WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.520
Obi-Wan Kenobi's whole existence in the Star&nbsp;
Wars universe is tied up with the fate of Anakin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.160
Skwalker — and their history is even longer&nbsp;
and more complicated than you might think.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.280
This is Obi-Wan's history&nbsp;
with Darth Vader explained.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.000
In The Phantom Menace, Obi-Wan tells his master,&nbsp;
Qui-Gon Jinn, that he senses they've "picked up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.360
another pathetic life form," referring to the&nbsp;
young Anakin Skywalker. This line demonstrates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.160
how, from the very beginning, Obi-Wan didn't&nbsp;
think they needed extra baggage on their quest to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.680
stop the Trade Federation's invasion of Naboo. In&nbsp;
fact, Obi-Wan and Anakin never seem to gel in The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.280
Phantom Menace. As Qui-Gon waits to hear if the&nbsp;
Jedi Council will accept Anakin as an apprentice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:47.760
Obi-Wan even points out that his master's defiance&nbsp;
is preventing his promotion to the Council itself.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.560
Obi-Wan strictly adheres to the Jedi code and&nbsp;
takes issue with Qui-Gon's constant rebellion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.920
against it. However, when Qui-Gon is killed by&nbsp;
Darth Maul, his dying request is that Obi-Wan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:03.760
train the young Anakin. Obi-Wan himself briefly&nbsp;
takes on Qui-Gon's rebellious spirit when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.360
tells Yoda he will train Anakin to fulfill this&nbsp;
wish, regardless of whether the Council approves.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.000
Obi-Wan's general fidelity&nbsp;
to the Jedi Order and its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.280
rules frequently contrasts with the older&nbsp;
Anakin's perpetual rebellion against them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.760
However, the decision to go against the Council&nbsp;
in the first place is handed down by Qui-Gon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.840
who planted a seed for the rift that&nbsp;
would one day tear the galaxy apart.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:33.120
From the start, Anakin Skywalker is depicted as a&nbsp;
man of action, while Obi-Wan is a more careful and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.720
analytical fighter. A perfect example of this&nbsp;
takes place in Attack of the Clones, when Anakin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:44.240
rushes in to fight Count Dooku, only to be knocked&nbsp;
out by his enemy's Force lightning. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:49.440
Obi-Wan chooses to take a more defensive approach&nbsp;
— and lasts longer in battle because of it.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.280
While Anakin is seen as something of&nbsp;
a prodigy, his reckless actions often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.240
lead Obi-Wan to regard his apprentice&nbsp;
with exasperation as well as admiration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.160
In the Clone Wars series, Obi-Wan&nbsp;
frequently scolds Anakin for being too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.400
fool-hardy while Anakin often calls&nbsp;
out Obi-Wan for being too hesitant.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.200
"We don't need a whole&nbsp;
fleet, I can do this myself."

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:15.360
"Anakin, slow down and do what I tell you. It's&nbsp;
more important to save lives than destroy ships."

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:20.400
Anakin leaps into battle without thinking&nbsp;
about it and, thanks to his abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.880
always makes it out on the other side. On&nbsp;
the other hand, Obi-Wan always tries to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:30.480
evaluate every situation in order to come up&nbsp;
with a proper plan. Of course, it's Anakin's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:36.000
reckless need to take action that eventually&nbsp;
leads him to the dark side. No doubt the older&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.280
Obi-Wan would have wished that he had taken this&nbsp;
character flaw of Anakin's far more seriously.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.480
A key facet of the Jedi code is&nbsp;
that Force users should always avoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.120
personal attachments. Anakin shows us why&nbsp;
this principle is so important because his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.640
love of Padmé allows Palpatine to manipulate him&nbsp;
into joining the Dark Side. However, Anakin's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:02.880
attachment to his relationships isn't exclusive&nbsp;
to Padmé. It also includes Obi-Wan himself.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:10.160
"Obi-Wan is a great mentor, as wise as&nbsp;
Master Yoda and as powerful as Master Windu."

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.160
Attack of the Clones demonstrates how deep their&nbsp;
relationship goes when Anakin sees Obi-Wan come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:22.080
under attack by droidekas. Anakin had earlier&nbsp;
pointed out that Obi-Wan is the closest thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.400
he has to a father, and he clearly wants&nbsp;
to save him from the droids — but he's torn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:32.080
between that desire and his duty to protect&nbsp;
Padmé. Thankfully, Padmé actually suggests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:37.600
trying to save Obi-Wan themselves, giving Anakin&nbsp;
the opportunity to set out to rescue his master.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.600
Of course, it is this shared mission&nbsp;
that cements Anakin and Padmé's love.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.720
After their rescue mission fails and the two are&nbsp;
sentenced to execution in a gladiatorial arena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.600
they share a kiss that later leads to marriage.&nbsp;
Anakin's inability to deny his personal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:56.640
relationships is a flaw in his Jedi mindset that&nbsp;
recurs throughout the prequel era, eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:02.160
leading to his fall from grace. His affection&nbsp;
for Obi-Wan is a central issue in this dynamic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.800
making the history that Anakin, Padmé,&nbsp;
and Obi-Wan share a very dangerous thing.

00:04:07.676 --> 00:04:13.520
The Phantom Menace ends with Obi-Wan as a full&nbsp;
Jedi Knight and Anakin as a Padawan. A decade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.920
later, Attack of the Clones ends with Anakin's&nbsp;
marriage and the beginning of the Clone Wars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:22.320
Following that, The Clone Wars covers the&nbsp;
three-year gap between Attack of the Clones and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:27.680
Revenge of the Sith. Given the amount of ground&nbsp;
the series covers, it has to be inferred that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.160
when the First Battle of Geonosis takes&nbsp;
place and the war begins, Anakin is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:37.520
immediately promoted to Jedi Knight, as both&nbsp;
he and Obi-Wan are generals in The Clone Wars.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:42.800
From that time on, Obi-Wan and Anakin are seen&nbsp;
as colleagues on more or less the same level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.640
and they are generally given the same&nbsp;
level of responsibility in most situations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.880
It's worth remembering, however, that&nbsp;
not only had Anakin just been promoted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:56.240
but he started his training considerably later&nbsp;
in life than most Jedi. If Anakin had bristled at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:02.480
Obi-Wan's instruction before, no doubt he really&nbsp;
resents any perceived seniority by this point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:07.360
Obi-Wan, however, never seems to begrudge the&nbsp;
fact that Anakin skips ahead to become his equal.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:13.040
Anakin Skywalker was supposed to be Obi-Wan's&nbsp;
student, and you would expect a master and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.400
student relationship to continue in some shape&nbsp;
or form even after their formal training ends.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.680
That certainly seems to be the&nbsp;
case with Yoda and his students,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:27.280
as even Count Dooku views his old master with&nbsp;
respect. Yet, perhaps because of Obi-Wan and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:32.000
Anakin's closeness in age, their equal&nbsp;
military ranks, and Anakin's exceptional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.640
strength with the Force, they become more&nbsp;
like brothers than a student and a teacher.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:41.920
By the time Anakin is a full-fledged Jedi, he&nbsp;
already seems to think of himself as superior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:47.360
to his master. Obi-Wan is constantly advising&nbsp;
prudence, while Anakin almost always thinks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:52.000
immediate action is the key to victory. This&nbsp;
difference leads to competition between the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:56.880
as they seek to prove that their approach is&nbsp;
better. Anakin is especially eager to prove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:01.760
that he's stronger than Obi-Wan, culminating&nbsp;
in their duel on Mustafar, in which Obi-Wan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:07.280
insists Anakin can't defeat him. The younger Jedi&nbsp;
acts rashly and is left for dead as a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.720
putting a final end to their&nbsp;
long and fateful sibling rivalry.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:16.000
Anakin tends to think that Obi-Wan is&nbsp;
a model of self-control, to the point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:21.120
where he mistakes Obi-Wan's adherence to the&nbsp;
austere Jedi lifestyle for a lack of emotion or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:25.760
passion. Yet we see in The Clone Wars that&nbsp;
Obi-Wan understands Anakin's longings more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:29.600
than Skywalker seemed to realize.&nbsp;
He simply doesn't give in to them.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:35.600
Take, for instance, Obi-Wan's history with Satine&nbsp;
Kryze, the ruler of Mandalore. Their relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:40.960
parallels the dynamic between Anakin and Padmé,&nbsp;
as Satine is also a strong woman and political&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:46.400
leader. One Clone Wars story arc reveals that&nbsp;
she and Obi-Wan once had a romantic connection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.760
though it's never clear if they&nbsp;
acted on those feelings. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:54.080
it's obvious Obi-Wan cares for her, and&nbsp;
perhaps if he and Anakin had discussed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:59.360
their forbidden romances it would have helped&nbsp;
steer Anakin away from his eventual downfall.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:04.560
Despite what Anakin might think, Obi-Wan also&nbsp;
questions the Jedi Order from time to time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:08.800
This is first seen when he tells Yoda he&nbsp;
will train Anakin no matter what the council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:13.840
decides — but it is also made apparent with&nbsp;
his reaction to the Jedi Order's vilification&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:19.440
of Ahsoka Tano for a crime he knows she did not&nbsp;
commit. The real difference between these two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:24.720
Jedi is how they handle their issues with the Jedi&nbsp;
Order. For all his power, Anakin never learns to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:30.240
control his emotions the way Obi-Wan does, despite&nbsp;
Obi-Wan's pleas for his former Padawan to do so.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:36.800
In Attack of the Clones, Anakin angrily complains&nbsp;
to Padmé that Obi-Wan is jealous and holding him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:42.160
back. Of course, this isn't the case at all.&nbsp;
Obi-Wan only ever wants the best for Anakin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:46.400
believing that, despite the boy's exceptional&nbsp;
skills with the Force, his Padawan needed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:51.440
mature emotionally in order to become a full&nbsp;
Jedi Knight. Obviously, Obi-Wan was right.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:56.480
Several times in The Clone Wars, Obi-Wan&nbsp;
tells Anakin to play a situation carefully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:01.440
only to watch as Anakin rashly springs into&nbsp;
action. Sometimes it works out, but other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:06.640
times his brash choices lead to high casualties,&nbsp;
or to Obi-Wan having to rescue the young Jedi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:12.000
What Anakin sees as Obi-Wan's jealousy is&nbsp;
actually his master's desire to guide him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:17.840
reach his full potential. Eventually, when Obi-Wan&nbsp;
confronts Darth Vader, the former apprentice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:23.200
tells Obi-Wan not to lecture him, insisting&nbsp;
that he sees through the lies of the Jedi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:28.080
By extension, he claims to see through the&nbsp;
supposed lies that Obi-Wan had told him to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:34.160
him from fulfilling his destiny. It's a tragic&nbsp;
misinterpretation of their entire relationship.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.240
In A New Hope, Obi-Wan says&nbsp;
this of Anakin Skywalker:

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:44.000
"He was the best star-pilot in&nbsp;
the galaxy and a cunning warrior."

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.120
More importantly, though, he adds:

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:48.880
"And he was a good friend…"

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:54.960
Anakin's inability to identify and control&nbsp;
his emotions was a weakness that Palpatine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.960 --> 00:09:00.080
easily exploited. On the other hand, Obi-Wan&nbsp;
may have felt a more profound love for Anakin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:04.320
than his apprentice felt for him, simply&nbsp;
remaining in control of those feelings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:08.800
Obi-Wan's heart breaks when he watches the&nbsp;
security footage of Anakin killing younglings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:13.040
and on Mustafar, Obi-Wan laments that&nbsp;
he has failed his young apprentice.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.840
Obi-Wan retreated to the life of a hermit&nbsp;
in order to hide from the Empire after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:22.480
destruction of the Jedi Order, but you can't&nbsp;
help but wonder whether he also exiled himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:28.720
as punishment for preventing Anakin from falling&nbsp;
to the dark side. When Obi-Wan appears in Rebels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:33.680
a deep sadness lingers over his bittersweet&nbsp;
victory against his longtime rival, Maul.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:39.360
In A New Hope, Darth Vader says that he feels&nbsp;
Obi-Wan's presence on the Death Star, so there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:45.520
can be doubt that Obi-Wan knew Vader was there as&nbsp;
well. He chooses to go alone on his mission, in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:51.120
part because the ever-contemplative Obi-Wan knows&nbsp;
he will have to confront his former apprentice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:55.760
Looking at their final showdown from this&nbsp;
point of view, it is a reasonable conclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.760
that Obi-Wan believes his sacrifice to&nbsp;
be penance for failing his old friend.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.920
After Anakin becomes Darth Vader, Obi-Wan&nbsp;
volunteers to watch over Luke on Tatooine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:09.360
He didn't have to do this, however.&nbsp;
Obi-Wan could have left Luke to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:12.720
raised by the Lars family alone.&nbsp;
Of course, he takes this mission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:17.440
in part out of a desire to see a Jedi&nbsp;
re-emerge and save the galaxy. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:23.120
another part of him probably wants to protect the&nbsp;
son of a friend he once cared very deeply for.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:27.840
When Obi-Wan tells Luke about his father in&nbsp;
A New Hope, he hides the true nature of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:32.560
relationship to Darth Vader, telling Luke that&nbsp;
Vader betrayed and murdered Anakin Skywalker.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:38.960
In Return of the Jedi, Obi-Wan famously claims&nbsp;
that Anakin ceased to exist once he became Vader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:42.240
and that what he told Luke was&nbsp;
true from a certain point of view.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:46.560
It stands to reason that Obi-Wan would have&nbsp;
held onto his feelings for his lost brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:50.880
and that he probably saw it as his&nbsp;
duty to watch over and protect his son.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:56.080
It's a well-known fact that Obi-Wan&nbsp;
won his victory over Anakin on Mustafar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:00.240
because of his ability to claim the&nbsp;
high ground. This slight difference in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:05.360
elevation allows Obi-Wan to slice off Anakin's&nbsp;
limbs after he attempts to go for the kill.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:10.480
However, this line applies to more than just the&nbsp;
physical difference between the two Jedi. Obi-Wan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:14.880
has also gained the moral high ground here,&nbsp;
and it's hard to argue otherwise — especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:19.120
considering that Anakin has just destroyed&nbsp;
the Jedi Order he was sworn to protect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:22.320
slaughtered the younglings,&nbsp;
and attacked his own wife.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:26.880
Throughout the prequels and the series,&nbsp;
Obi-Wan has a firmer grasp of morality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:32.080
and duty than Anakin, who often acts for selfish&nbsp;
reasons. And while more stories in the Star Wars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:37.200
galaxy may find Obi-Wan struggling with the&nbsp;
moral ambiguities of life outside the order,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:40.960
he will no doubt always keep the high&nbsp;
ground over his former apprentice.

